WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.334 --> 00:00:01.491
(tense string music)

00:00:01.491 --> 00:00:03.148
- [Soldier] We've tapped
into their radios.

00:00:03.148 --> 00:00:05.410
We can confirm two divisions.

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:07.050
- [General] Confirmed.
We have an aerial visual.

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:08.422
- [Soldier] Copy?

00:00:08.422 --> 00:00:10.694
- [General] Yes, yes, we
can hear them moving in.

00:00:10.694 --> 00:00:13.000
- [Host] Only none of what the Germans

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.333
thought they could see or hear was real.

00:00:17.437 --> 00:00:20.158
During World War II, a secret
division of the US Army,

00:00:20.158 --> 00:00:23.325
now known as the Ghost
Army, conducted over 20

00:00:23.325 --> 00:00:25.893
tactical operations, which resulted in

00:00:25.893 --> 00:00:28.514
saving tens of thousands of lives.

00:00:28.514 --> 00:00:29.511
The mission?

00:00:29.511 --> 00:00:31.671
To trick the enemy into
thinking that their unit

00:00:31.671 --> 00:00:36.530
of 1,000 men was actually
two divisions of 30,000 men.

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:39.598
But the Ghost Army wasn't made
up of traditional soldiers.

00:00:39.598 --> 00:00:43.027
The majority were actors,
designers, advertisers,

00:00:43.027 --> 00:00:45.604
and artists who had been
recruited from the top

00:00:45.604 --> 00:00:48.463
art and design schools around the country.

00:00:48.463 --> 00:00:50.945
And this army of artists
used their creativity

00:00:50.945 --> 00:00:53.278
for an infantry of illusion.

00:00:54.195 --> 00:00:56.834
Engineers developed inflatable tanks

00:00:56.834 --> 00:00:59.388
which the artists would then paint.

00:00:59.388 --> 00:01:02.327
These tanks could condense
down to fit into a portable bag

00:01:02.327 --> 00:01:07.059
and inflate on demand,
much like a bouncy castle.

00:01:07.059 --> 00:01:10.383
Audio engineers used large
speakers to play sound effects

00:01:10.383 --> 00:01:12.310
of tanks and marching soldiers,

00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:15.246
which had been pre-recorded at Fort Knox.

00:01:15.246 --> 00:01:18.813
This marching army could
be heard from miles away.

00:01:18.813 --> 00:01:21.782
Along with fake radio
messages sent into the signals

00:01:21.782 --> 00:01:24.204
of the enemies, they
would also send actors

00:01:24.204 --> 00:01:27.143
dressed as generals and
officers into local towns

00:01:27.143 --> 00:01:30.140
to spread false information and rumors.

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:34.072
It wasn't until 1996, when
information about the Ghost Army

00:01:34.072 --> 00:01:36.668
was declassified that
the world finally knew

00:01:36.668 --> 00:01:38.907
about these masters of misdirection,

00:01:38.907 --> 00:01:41.740
the unsung heroes of World War II.

